            <ArticleTitle>Results of elective stenting of branch-ostial lesions.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>472-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Coronary stenting using both Palmaz-Schatz and Gianturco-Roubin stents for branch ostial lesions was performed in 48 patients with high success and low complication rates. The 6-month event-free survival rates were high in these patients.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
